"""Stub for the ``temper_orchestration`` extension (temper-orchestration
crate, Wave-4 Phase-5 cli/adapters/temper-workflow slice).

Mirrors the temper_design_bundle_python stub convention: the pyo3 extension
is imported by the delegation shims (``temper_placer.cli.timing``,
``temper_placer.cli.trace_commands``,
``temper_workflow.routing.route_and_measure``); the mypy gate resolves this
stub through ``mypy_path = "packages/temper-placer/stubs"``.

The crate grew from that first Wave-4 Phase-5 slice into the Rust
Orchestration Engine (plan 2026-08-09-001, U0 through E6/tail-tooling,
"Append-only per the U4 dispatch") across many incremental PRs, each landing
new ``#[pyclass]``/``#[pyfunction]`` entries in ``lib.rs``'s ``#[pymodule]``
block without a matching stub update -- the entries below (2026-08-12,
type-check gate paydown) close that gap by mirroring ``lib.rs`` exactly.
Signatures are permissive (``*args``/``**kwargs`` -> ``Any``) rather than
precisely typed, matching this file's own pre-existing convention for the
feasibility kernels below and ``decision_contracts.pyi``'s convention for
bare pyclasses: the goal is closing "Module has no attribute" / "not valid
as a type" mypy errors from a stub that fell behind an append-only Rust
surface, not re-deriving each stage's exact call signature. Keep in sync
with ``packages/temper-orchestration/src/lib.rs``'s ``#[pymodule]`` block.
"""

